The fire department shall comprise the fire chief and any firefighters or other employees as necessary. The purpose of the fire department is to:
(a) Protect life and property against fire, explosions, hazardous materials, or electrical hazards;
(b) Detect and prevent arson;
(c) Administer and enforce the laws of this state; the rules and regulations adopted by the department, agencies of the state; and City ordinances, rules, regulations, or codes related to the prevention and suppression of fires, explosions, or injuries from hazardous materials and explosions and the protection of life and property from such hazards;
(d) Conduct programs of public education in fire prevention and safety;
(e) Conduct emergency medical services and rescue assistance;
(f) Control and regulate the flow of traffic in areas of existing emergencies, including rail, highway, water, and air traffic; and
(g) Perform all such services of a fire department as may be provided by law or which necessarily appertain thereto.
The fire department may be assisted by others as authorized by the mayor and council, fire chief, or as provided in any duly executed intergovernmental contract or mutual aid agreement.
(Ord. 2023-07-13, § 1, Added 07/10/2023)
State Law reference— General powers and duties of local governments with respect to fire departments, O.C.G.A. §§ 25-3-1 et seq.

